JavaScript Fundamentals
JavaScript is a programming language used to make web pages interactive and dynamic.
It works together with:
HTML → Structure
CSS → Design
JavaScript → Behavior / Logic

1. Variables
Variables are used to store data.
JavaScript provides three keywords:
let → value can be changed
const → value cannot be reassigned
var → older way of declaring variables
Example
let name = "Pritish";
let age = 28;

console.log(name);
console.log(age);
Changing a variable
let marks = 50;

marks = 80;

console.log(marks);
Output:
80
const
const pi = 3.14;

console.log(pi);
You cannot do:
pi = 4;
Best practice
Use:
const
when the value doesn't need reassignment, and:
let
when it does.

