Comparison Operators
Used to compare two values.
let a = 10;
let b = 20;

console.log(a == b);
console.log(a != b);
console.log(a > b);
console.log(a < b);
console.log(a >= b);
console.log(a <= b);
===
=== checks both value and data type.
console.log(10 === 10);
Output:
true
console.log(10 === "10");
Output:
false
For modern JavaScript, prefer === and !== for comparisons.

